    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d805">

                <pb facs="1568" n="1528" xml:id="pg1528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.86/4–2054: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 805<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Saudi Arabia (Wadsworth)
                        to the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-20T13:00:00+03:00">April 20, 1954—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>440. Deptel 290, April 15.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d805-f1"/> From our listening
                    post in this primitive still basically puritanical Wahabi community in which St.
                    John Philby tells me Court thinking continues governed largely by old King’s
                    theme that SA is “firstly Moslem and only secondly Arab” we can best answer
                    question in referenced telegram by saying we see no procedure for getting
                    parties together for any purpose and question two by reporting that not even our
                    generally well informed Embassy Arab consultant has ever heard of UNTSO or
                    bothers even endeavor comprehend details border machinery.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wadsworth</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
